{"title":"25 Years of Epic Bikepark Leogang, Skills with Elements & Bike Festival This Weekend","link":"https://bikerumor.com/25-years-of-epic-bikepark-leogang-skills-with-elements-bike-festival-this-weekend/","date":1790917200000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/25-Years-of-Leogang_passive-drop-training-with-Elements-Bike-School-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"&lt;i&gt;(All photos/Cory Benson)&lt;/i&gt;\" /></p>\n<p>Marking their 25th year as one of the longest-running and most popular gravity MTB destinations in Europe, we dropped in for the second time this season at The Epic Bikepark Leogang last week. It’s always a great spot to test out some of the latest mountain bike gear on killer alpine trails and the world-renowned DH track. More on those later. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>But we also had a few other ulterior motives. Like a quick chance to hone some skills with the Elements Bike School instructors, and to chat with the shapers who build and maintain the trails for an upcoming Trail Tools story we have in the works. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Plus, while enjoying sunny summer weather late in the season, it was a good reminder that Bike Festival is coming to Leogang this coming weekend…</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>The Epic Bikepark Leogang: 25 Epic Years On</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-scaled.jpg\" alt=\"Epic Bikepark Leogang 25 Years: iconic DH track\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/iconic-Leogang-Speedway-and-Flying-Gangster-tunnels-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(Photos/Cory Benson)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s kind of hard to fathom that the Leogang bikepark has been running for a quarter century. In fact, it was at another iconic European mountain bike destination where I came to this realization (<em>and a reminder of aging and the passing of time!</em>) Back in early March, I was testing out new tires, wheels, suspension, and (<em>importantly</em>) protection in Finale Ligure when I happened to end up in the same backcountry uplift as Martin Samek. The <a href=\"https://www.trailwerk.at/\">Trailwerk Wachau</a> founder’s diploma thesis had been the impetus for the creation of the Leogang bikepark back in 2000 – a collaboration between the ski lift operator, the local town, tourism board, a local earthworks contractor, and several other supporters. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>In 2001, Epic Bikepark Leogang became the first bikepark in Austria with just 4 trails – mostly catering to an elite group of expert mountain bikers. In the two and a half decades since, the big jump lines and pro-level downhill tracks are still a big focus. The park has since hosted 2x UCI MTB World Championships and 14x UCI MTB World Cup races, including DH, XC, Enduro, and even the occasional short track, 4x, dual slalom, and eliminator. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>But now, we’re likely to see a much wider skill range of mountain bikers in the iconic blue gondolas – now including a healthy dose of ebikers, entry-level trail riders &amp; kids, in addition to shredders heading for the Hot Shots jump line. Me personally, I prefer the more natural lines – call them enduro singletracks – and the classic down &amp; dirty bikepark tracks like the recently updated Hangman I.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Bikerumor testing tracks and World Cup prototype proving ground…</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots.jpg\"><img width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots.jpg\" alt=\"2026 Maxxis Minion DHX x New DH gravity mountain bike tire, tested at Leogang\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Maxxis-Minion-DHX-gravity-MTB-tire-with-all-new-dry-conditions-tread-and-reinforced-New-DH-casing_photo-by-Joao-Reis_Hangman-roots-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption>previewing new Maxxis Minion DHX with New DH casing on Hangman I <i>(Photo by Joao Reis/Maxxis)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>In any case, Leogang lives on as an excellent spot to test new gear like the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/maxxis-debuts-a-new-minion-dhx-for-dry-plus-all-new-dh-casing-for-all-first-riding-review/\" target=\"_blank\">latest Maxxis DHX</a> with its New DH casing. Or Schwalbe’s <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/review-schwalbe-albert-gravity-trail-radial-mtb-tires-simply-grip-more/\" target=\"_blank\">Radial casing tires</a> before that. Then, Leatt’s <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/bikerumor-editors-choice-2024-cory-best-bike-and-gear-awards/\">ReaFlex Chest/Back Protector &amp; X-Flow goggles</a> before that. Or even the previous generation of Scott’s <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/2022-scott-spark-gets-bold-new-redesign-as-a-slack-fast-fully-integrated-120mm-xc-bike/\" target=\"_blank\">Spark XC &amp; downcountry bikes</a>, years earlier.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/2024-Editors-Choice-Cory-Benson_Saalbach-riding-in-a-cloud-jpg.webp\"><img width=\"1500\" height=\"2000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/u